\fs46 \
The Ring-Match tool can be invoked from the bottom control bar. \
\
\
For best results:\
	\'95 listen with headphones (wired or wireless)\
	\'95 go to the quietest possible environment, away from external noise.\
	\'95 start with a \ul very low volume\ulnone \
	\'95 begin by auditioning the different frequency bands (upper-bass, lower-mid, midrange, upper-mid, etc).\
	\'95 increase (or decrease) the volume only enough to match the volume of your internal ringing.\
	\'95 preview all the frequency bands and choose the one that most matches the \'91area\'92 (band) of your ringing.\
	\'95 click \'93EXPAND\'94 to drill down further.\
	\'95 here you can drill-down and preview the sub-frequencies, listening closely for which one comes the closest to matching your ringing frequency.\
	\'95 TIP:  try shorter bursts (toggling each on/off), and notice that \ul you may actually experience a momentary relief\ulnone . Notice which specific frequency burst inspires the biggest temporary relief. This can be your starting point.\
	\'95 Chose \'93SELECT\'94 for the one that gives you the most (temporary) relief.\
	\'95 This frequency will be retained within your app.
